{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And Lamech said to his wives</b> — The commentators (Rashi and Ibn Ezra) based their interpretation of this matter on the view of Onkelos, who explained “Therefore whoever kills Cain, vengeance shall be taken on him sevenfold” (Genesis 4:15) to mean that for seven generations vengeance will be exacted from him, but not now, for HaShem prolonged His anger against him. Now Lamech's wives feared to bear children because they would be seventh-generation descendants of Cain, and he consoled his wives that HaShem would prolong his life another seventy-seven years, for he would pray before Him since He is slow to anger and would have mercy on him — or else it was a foolish *kal va-chomer* (argument from minor to major) according to the midrash that Rashi mentioned (Rashi on Genesis 4:24). If so, he says: therefore whoever kills Cain — vengeance shall be taken from him sevenfold, meaning in his own days, and this is the translation of Onkelos: “כל דיקטול קין לשבעה דרין יתפרע מניה” (whoever kills Cain, for seven generations it will be avenged from him). And if so, “And Lamech said to his wives” should have been placed earlier.\n\nIn my opinion, however, “sevenfold” does not mean seven generations, for this term is not used for seven separate things but rather for the sevenfold multiplication of a single thing, as in “purified seven times” (Psalms 12:7), “he shall repay sevenfold” (Proverbs 6:31), “and the light of the sun shall be sevenfold” (Isaiah 30:26) — doubled and multiplied seven parts.\n\nRather, the meaning of “whoever kills Cain” is as its plain sense: HaShem said, therefore whoever kills Cain, sevenfold vengeance shall be taken from him — I will punish the one who kills him seven times for his sin, for I promised Cain that he would not be killed on account of his fear of Me and his confession before Me.\n\nBut the matter of Lamech with his wives, the Scripture did not mention in explanation. We may also say that they feared the punishment that Lamech might be killed for the iniquity of his father, for HaShem did not say to Cain, “I have forgiven you,” but only that he would not be killed — yet His debt would be exacted from his seed, and they did not know when. And so indeed the matter came to pass.\n\nAnd Lamech consoled them, saying that HaShem would have mercy upon him as He had mercy upon Cain, for he is innocent of bloodshed, and he too would pray before Him and He would hear his prayer.\n\nBut what seems right to me is that Lamech was a very wise man in every craft of ingenuity. He taught his firstborn the matter of herding according to the nature of animals, and he taught the second the art of music, and he taught the third to forge and make swords and spears and javelins and all weapons of war. And his wives were afraid that he would be punished because he brought the sword and murder into the world, and behold he holds the deed of his fathers in his hand, for he is the son of the first murderer and has created a weapon of destruction to maim. And he said to them: I have not killed a man for wounds, nor a child for bruises, as Cain did, and HaShem will not punish me, but will protect me from being killed even more than him.\n\nAnd he mentioned this to say that it is not with sword and spear that a man can kill, for with wounds and bruises one can cause a death worse than the sword, and the sword does not cause murder, and there is no sin upon its maker."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "In the midrash Rashi cites (on Genesis 4:24), Lamech's wives separated from him after he accidentally killed Cain (who was still alive after seven generations). The 'foolish kal va-chomer' refers to Lamech's argument: if Cain, who killed one person, was given a sevenfold protection, then Lamech, who killed two (Cain and Tubal-cain, his own son, per the midrash), deserves seventy-sevenfold protection."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:25:06.490558342Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}